## Interface
-- Interface in java is defined is used to as abstract type is used to behaviour of method
-- interface is blueprint/prototype of behaviour of method
-- an interface contains static constant and abstract methods.
-- an interface is a set of rule that defines whats methods are implements should have bit it doesnot define how these methods are implements.
-- A class that implements the interface must provide the code for these methods.
Example:- Realife example:= 
Payment system:-
Different method like credit cards upi or Paypal can implement a payment method interface. this way all payment method follow the same rule but process payment in their own way,

Note :- interace only define whats need to done, not how to do it.

class -----> to ------> class ====> Extends 
class ------> to _-------> Interface ===> implements
Interface ------> to _-------> Interface ===>  Extends

interface Shape {
    void calArea();
}

class Square implements Shape {
    public void calArea() {
        int side = 5;
        System.out.println(side * side);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Square s = new Square();
        s.calArea();
    }
}
